#!/bin/sh
''''[ -n "${THIMBLE_SESSION:-}" ] && [ -n "${THIMBLE_SESSION_TOKEN:-}" ] && exit 0; h="${THIMBLE_HOME:-$HOME/.thimble}"; case "${1:-}" in --stream|--scratch|--work-budget) ;; --rekey) [ -z "${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-}" ] || [ ${#CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR} -gt 200 ] || [ -e "$h/active/$(printf %s "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR" | tr / %)" ] || exit 0;; *) if [ -n "${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID:-}" ]; then [ -e "$h/up/$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID.active" ] || exit 0; else [ -z "${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR:-}" ] || [ ${#CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR} -gt 200 ] || [ -e "$h/active/$(printf %s "$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR" | tr / %)" ] || exit 0; fi;; esac; exec "$(dirname "$0")/thimble-python" -S "$0" "$@" # '''
"""thimble's watcher: how thimble's events reach the analyst's Claude Code session, and how its hooks follow the
session. The plugin's hooks (plugin/hooks/hooks.json) run it, and where those hooks are off (the Monitor route) main's
Monitor does.

The first two lines make this file both a shell script and a Python program, as in bin/thimble-mcp; the shell line
exits at once in a session thimble starts itself, which has THIMBLE_SESSION and the THIMBLE_SESSION_TOKEN that proves it
(app/hook_auth.py), since Claude Code's background service can hand the name alone on to the user's own sessions.
Python runs with -S, since the file uses only the standard library and runs on every tool call.

The shell line is also a gate, since the plugin's hooks run in every Claude Code session on the machine: in a session
thimble is not on in, a hook exits before Python starts. Thimble is on in a session when <thimble home>/up/<session
id>.active exists, the session marker activation writes (app/activate.py), named by CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, which
Claude Code gives its hooks. Where it gives none, the gate falls back to the folder's marker: an empty file in <thimble
home>/active named for the folder's path (CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR) with each `/` made `%`, which activation writes for the
folder and for its real path (app/cli.py mark_active) and `thimble rm` takes away (app/runs.py purge); a hook passes it
when Claude Code names no folder, and for a folder path over 200 characters, for which no marker is written. --rekey,
whose session is new and has no marker yet, meets the folder's gate; --stream, --scratch and --work-budget never meet
the gate, since only main's Monitor and the sessions of an extension's program run them, where thimble put them.

    .thimble-watch                      the asyncRewake hook (SessionStart, Stop, PreToolUse, UserPromptSubmit)
    .thimble-watch --permission         the PermissionRequest hook: tells the server a prompt waits, decides nothing
    .thimble-watch --held               the UserPromptSubmit hook that adds the events held for main to the prompt
                                        and prints the lines of the events the watcher wrote out
    .thimble-watch --mode               the UserPromptSubmit and Stop hook that reports the session's permission mode
    .thimble-watch --agents             the PostToolUse hook that tells thimble's agents and their descendants the ref
                                        of each call and when their work folder grows past its budget, and tells main
                                        to end its turn on a start it launched
    .thimble-watch --agent-check        the PreToolUse hook of Agent and SendMessage calls, main's and its subagents'
    .thimble-watch --subagent-start     the SubagentStart hook: registers one of thimble's agents or a descendant
    .thimble-watch --subagent-stop      the SubagentStop hook: a registered agent's turn ended
    .thimble-watch --caller             the PreToolUse hook of thimble's tools: which agent makes the call
    .thimble-watch --denied             the PermissionDenied hook: auto mode refused a start or a message (R1)
    .thimble-watch --end                the SessionEnd hook: main's end
    .thimble-watch --rekey              the SessionStart hook for clear and resume: the session marker and the agents
                                        move to the new session
    .thimble-watch --scratch --work <folder> --text <line>
    .thimble-watch --work-budget --work <folder> --budget <bytes> --text <line>
                                        the SubagentStart and PostToolUse hooks of an extension's program session
                                        (app/agent_session.py scratch_hooks)
    .thimble-watch --stream --cwd <folder> --session <id>
                                        the Monitor route

The hooks of thimble's agents (--agent-check, --subagent-start, --subagent-stop, --caller, --denied, --end, --rekey)
write their record to the workspace's files first, under a file lock (app/subagent_files.py: subagents.json and
callers.jsonl), and post to the server only when server.json names one; --agent-check decides from subagents.json alone.
They find the workspace from the session's folder as the server does, importing app/subagent_files.py from the tree
(which is standard library only). Each hook reads the session's transport from the workspace's launch.json
(app/subagent_files.py transport): local until a press of the browser workbench, and for a peer, where it uses the
workspace's files alone (below); the server's after the press, where every other hook but the stream does nothing
without $THIMBLE_HOME/server.json and the token in it, and nothing switches back when the server is gone. Each request proves it holds the token and each answer must prove the server does (app/hook_auth.py); an
answer without that proof counts as no server, so a process on the recorded port is neither told anything nor believed.

The hook long-polls the server for the session's next event (GET /api/events/pull), writes it to stderr in the
`<thimble-event …>` form, acknowledges it and exits 2, which makes Claude Code wake the session. It exits 0 in a
subagent, when another watcher holds the session's lock, when no server listens at first, on 404/410 (STOP), when the
`claude` process has moved to another session (/clear), and when that process has exited. A server that has answered
once is waited for across restarts.

The permission hook only tells the server, after a press, that a prompt waits (POST /api/events/permission, which shows
it on main's card without buttons), and prints nothing: thimble makes no allow decision, and Claude Code asks in its own
dialog. On local transport it tells no one.

The held hook runs as each of main's turns begins, on a prompt the analyst typed and on an event the watcher woke it
with: it takes the events the server holds for main (app/events.py QUIET_KINDS) and prints them as the prompt's added
context, and prints the lines main's terminal shows of the events the watcher wrote out (app/events.py terminal_line)
as its systemMessage, since Claude Code shows such an event only as the fixed rewakeSummary. It prints nothing in a
subagent, when nothing waits or when no server answers within HELD_WAIT_S. It never blocks a prompt: the hand-back of one
of thimble's agents, and in default mode a later run's task notification, reach main as Claude Code sends them, and
main replies in one line (prompts/main.md).

The mode hook tells the server (POST /api/events/mode) the permission mode Claude Code reports for the session as each
of its turns begins and ends, which is the mode the agents thimble starts follow by default. It sends nothing in a
subagent. The first time main reports Manual mode in a session, the server answers with a line that says so and how to
switch to auto mode (app/modes.py manual_line), which the hook shows as its systemMessage. As a turn ends it also shows,
once, the dashboard link `server up` left for the session (app/cli.py leave_link): the link carries a sign-in code the
server makes as the hook shows it, which works once, for 5 minutes, until a newer one for the workspace is made
(app/hook_auth.py); a systemMessage reaches the analyst's terminal but not the model's context, and Claude Code also
records it in the session's transcript. The server also leaves notes here with no link, such as the line for a new
sign-in (app/session.py tell_terminal). Both go in one systemMessage, the link first.

The agents hook tells one of thimble's agents, or a descendant of one, the ref of each call it made (POST
/api/ws/<c>/calls/ref, for the orientation and its descendants, whose calls its thread numbers) and, after a Bash call,
when the work folder of its thimble ancestor holds more than WORK_BUDGET (`## work-budget` of prompts/tools.md), at most
once per budget step and every CHECK_S. For main it prints only after main's own Agent call launched a thread's fork or
one of thimble's agents: the note that the turn ends on that call (app/subagent_files.py launched_note, `## agent-launched`),
since Claude Code's launch result asks main to go on, and main then made a call that does nothing or the same start again.
After an Agent call, main's or a subagent's, that launched one of thimble's agents, it records that agent as the one the
call started (app/subagent_files.py settle): the SubagentStart hook cannot tell apart two agents of one type started in
one turn, so such an agent waits for this record, or for the call's result in main's transcript, to take up its start.

The agent-check hook runs on main's Agent and SendMessage calls and on those of its subagents (app/subagent_files.py
check_call): it lets a start of one of thimble's roles through only when it matches a pending request exactly, records a
subagent's Agent call as a nested start, denies a SendMessage to one of thimble's agents that no pending message request
names (but not a subagent's to its own parent), and asks the server (POST /api/bg/agent-check) only whether main's
Agent call would start a second fork of a thread. It never answers allow and never rewrites the call. The waker exits
at once in `claude -p` (main's command line has -p or --print), which would otherwise wait for it and never call the
model.

Local transport (the session's transport in launch.json: before a press, and always for a peer) has no server, and no
hook makes an HTTP request there. The file-first hooks write their record as after a press and then start the
backend's call for it, `thimble-python -m app.local_hooks <kind>` with the hook's input, detached, in place of the post
(spawn_local; app/local_hooks.py), and the SubagentStop hook starts it for every subagent, so that the mirror reads a
thread's fork too. --agent-check also refuses a second fork of a thread from subagents.json (app/subagent_files.py
fork_check), and records each fork it lets through by its tool_use id, by which the mirror knows the fork's thread.
The waker polls the workspace's events/queue.jsonl (app/event_files.py) for an event of its own session that no watcher
has taken (an event names its session, and one that names none is main's), takes it, writes it to stderr and exits 2;
once a press turned its session's transport to the server, it pulls from the server with the session's lock it holds,
since no other hook's waker runs while main is idle (the `thimble` command presses at the session's start).
--held prints the session's held events from held-events.json and the lines of the events the waker wrote out.
--mode records main's permission mode in subagents.json, and when it turns into or out of Manual mode starts the
backend's `mode-notice` call, which shows or clears the `manual-mode` notice in the terminal UI's band
(app/notices.py); on main's Stop it starts the backend's `main-stop` call. Plan mode stops none of thimble's running
agents (Claude Code's own subagents go on in plan mode). --agents numbers an orientation's calls in its sequence
(app/calls_file.py) and gives the ref as the server would.

--rekey (SessionStart for clear and resume) moves the session that ended in this `claude` process (the SessionEnd
hook's record, --end) to the new session: its agents (app/subagent_files.py rekey), and its marker with the folder of
its session files (rekey_marker): for /resume the marker and every file as they were, the guidance's record and its
guide marker kept, and the session's coverage facts copied; for /clear the marker with an empty guidance record and a
new guide marker, so the guidance is owed again, and no coverage facts. A marker the new session has already (the
terminal UI's activation ran first) is left as it is.

The stream writes each event as one block of lines. Claude Code truncates Monitor output at 500 characters per line and
about 3,000 per event, so lines are wrapped under LINE_CHARS and a longer event is cut and saved whole under
<thimble home>/events/.
"""
import fcntl
import hashlib
import hmac
import http.client
import json
import os
import re
import secrets
import sys
import time
import urllib.error
import urllib.parse
import urllib.request
from pathlib import Path

PULL_WAIT_S = 25  # app/events.py PULL_WAIT_S: the server holds a pull this long
LIFETIME_S = 23 * 3600  # the hook's own timeout is 86400 s (hooks.json)
RETRY_S = 2.0
LOCK_SWEEP_S = 2 * 86400  # a lock file untouched this long belongs to no running watcher (each takes it anew)
MAX_HOPS = 8  # claude_pid's walk up the process tree
STREAM_CHARS = 2_800  # below Claude Code's cut of a Monitor event
LINE_CHARS = 480  # below Claude Code's cut of a Monitor line, 500, counted as it counts (UTF-16 code units)
SPACE = re.compile(r" ")
ATTR_BREAK = re.compile(r' (?=[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=")')  # the space before an attribute (a value's " is escaped)
WAKE = 2  # the exit code that wakes the session (asyncRewake)
STOP = {404, 410}  # the server's answers that end a watcher (module note)
CUT_NOTE = "(cut here, since a Monitor event holds about 3,000 characters; the whole event is in {path})"
END_TAG = "</thimble-event>"  # closes an event as the server renders it (app/events.py render)
HELD_WAIT_S = 3.0
AGENTS_WAIT_S = 3.0
PERMISSION_WAIT_S = 2.0  # how long the permission hook's note to the server may take; Claude Code's dialog waits for it
PAIR_WAIT_S = 3.0  # how long the Stop hook waits for the link's sign-in code (link_lines)
NO_CODE_LINE = "thimble: to sign this browser in, run `thimble up` in a shell and open the link it prints."
# every request goes to thimble's own server on 127.0.0.1, never through a proxy the shell names
LOOPBACK = urllib.request.build_opener(urllib.request.ProxyHandler({}))


def home() -> Path:
    return Path(os.environ.get("THIMBLE_HOME") or (Path.home() / ".thimble"))


def server() -> tuple[str, str] | None:
    """(the server's API base URL, its token) from $THIMBLE_HOME/server.json (`api`, then `port`, as bin/thimble-mcp
    reads it); None without the file or a token."""
    try:
        data = json.loads((home() / "server.json").read_text("utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    token = data.get("token") if isinstance(data, dict) else None
    if not isinstance(token, str) or not token:
        return None
    try:
        if data.get("api"):
            return str(data["api"]).rstrip("/"), token
        if data.get("port"):
            return f"http://127.0.0.1:{int(data['port'])}", token
    except (TypeError, ValueError):
        pass
    return None


class NoServer(urllib.error.URLError):
    """No thimble server to ask: no server.json or token, or an answer without the server's proof (module note)."""


def sign(token: str, role: str, nonce: str) -> str:
    """app/hook_auth.py's sign: the proof `role` gives for `nonce` (the server's, on an answer)."""
    return hmac.new(token.encode("utf-8"), f"{role}:{nonce}".encode("utf-8"), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()


def proof_headers(token: str, base: str) -> dict[str, str]:
    """app/hook_auth.py's headers: a fresh nonce (its new_nonce) and the request's proof for the port `base` names (its
    request_proof), good on that port alone, for a few minutes, once."""
    nonce = f"{int(time.time())}.{secrets.token_hex(16)}"
    port = urllib.parse.urlsplit(base).port or 80
    auth = hmac.new(token.encode("utf-8"), f"hook@{port}:{nonce}".encode("utf-8"), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()
    return {"X-Thimble-Nonce": nonce, "X-Thimble-Auth": auth}


def request(method: str, path: str, body: dict | None = None, timeout: float | None = 10.0,
            proven: bool = True) -> tuple[int, dict]:
    """(status, JSON body) of one request to the server, with this hook's proof; an HTTP error is its status. NoServer,
    a urllib.error.URLError, when there is no server to ask or, unless not `proven`, its answer lacks the server's proof.
    A transport failure raises urllib.error.URLError when no connection was made, else another OSError or an
    http.client.HTTPException."""
    found = server()
    if found is None:
        raise NoServer("no server.json with a token")
    base, token = found
    proof_of = proof_headers(token, base)
    nonce = proof_of["X-Thimble-Nonce"]
    data = json.dumps(body).encode("utf-8") if body is not None else None
    headers = {**proof_of, **({"Content-Type": "application/json"} if data else {})}
    req = urllib.request.Request(base + path, data=data, method=method, headers=headers)
    try:
        with LOOPBACK.open(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:  # noqa: S310 — loopback, thimble's own server
            raw = resp.read()
            status = resp.status
            proof = resp.headers.get("X-Thimble-Proof") or ""
    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:
        raw, status, proof = b"", e.code, (e.headers.get("X-Thimble-Proof") if e.headers else None) or ""
    if proven and not hmac.compare_digest(proof, sign(token, "server", nonce)):
        raise NoServer("the answer does not carry thimble's proof")
    try:
        parsed = json.loads(raw.decode("utf-8")) if raw else {}
    except ValueError:
        parsed = {}
    return status, parsed if isinstance(parsed, dict) else {}


def hook_input() -> dict:
    try:
        data = json.loads(sys.stdin.read() or "{}")
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return {}
    return data if isinstance(data, dict) else {}


def folder(inp: dict) -> str:
    return os.environ.get("CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR") or str(inp.get("cwd") or "") or os.getcwd()


def lock(session: str):
    """This session's watcher lock, held for the process's life; None when another watcher holds it."""
    d = home() / "watch"
    try:
        d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        now = time.time()
        for p in d.glob("*.lock"):  # old sessions' files, which no watcher can still hold
            try:
                if now - p.stat().st_mtime > LOCK_SWEEP_S:
                    p.unlink()
            except OSError:
                pass
        f = open(d / f"{''.join(ch for ch in session if ch.isalnum() or ch in '-_')}.lock", "a")  # noqa: SIM115
        fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except OSError:
        return None
    os.utime(f.name)
    return f


def sessions_dir() -> Path:
    return Path(os.environ.get("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR") or (Path.home() / ".claude")) / "sessions"


def parent(pid: int) -> int:
    """The parent of `pid`, 0 when unknown: /proc where there is one, else ps (macOS)."""
    try:
        return int(Path(f"/proc/{pid}/stat").read_text().rsplit(")", 1)[1].split()[1])
    except (OSError, ValueError, IndexError):
        pass
    import subprocess  # noqa: PLC0415 — only without CLAUDE_PID and /proc: the hot path (each tool call) never needs it
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["ps", "-o", "ppid=", "-p", str(pid)], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=2).stdout
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return 0
    return int(out.strip()) if out.strip().isdigit() else 0


def claude_pid() -> int | None:
    """The `claude` process this watcher runs under: CLAUDE_PID, which Claude Code sets for its hooks and the commands
    it runs, else the nearest ancestor that has a session record in Claude Code's config directory, as
    app/cc_plugin.py's claude_pid finds it; None when neither says."""
    named = os.environ.get("CLAUDE_PID") or ""
    if named.isdigit():
        return int(named)
    pid = os.getppid()
    for _ in range(MAX_HOPS):
        if pid <= 1:
            return None
        if (sessions_dir() / f"{pid}.json").is_file():
            return pid
        pid = parent(pid)
    return None


def alive(pid: int) -> bool:
    try:
        os.kill(pid, 0)
    except ProcessLookupError:
        return False
    except PermissionError:
        pass
    return True


def process_session(pid: int | None) -> str | None:
    """The session the `claude` process `pid` runs now, from Claude Code's record of it, which /clear rewrites (module
    note); None when unknown."""
    if not pid:
        return None
    try:
        data = json.loads((sessions_dir() / f"{pid}.json").read_text("utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    sid = data.get("sessionId") if isinstance(data, dict) else None
    return sid if isinstance(sid, str) and sid else None


def pull(cwd: str, session: str, until: float, pid: int | None = None, *,
         follow: bool = False) -> tuple[str, str, str] | None:
    """(id, text, session) of the next event, None when the watcher should stop (module note). A refused connection
    before any answer is a stop; once a server has answered or taken a request, it is waited for until `until`. With the
    process's `pid`, each poll first looks at the session the process runs now: the stream (`follow`) polls for that
    one, and a hook's watcher whose session the process has left (/clear) stops."""
    reached = False
    while time.monotonic() < until:
        if pid and not alive(pid):
            return None
        now = process_session(pid)
        if now and now != session:
            if not follow:
                return None
            session = now
        query = urllib.parse.urlencode({k: v for k, v in (("cwd", cwd), ("session", session), ("pid", pid),
                                                          ("wait", PULL_WAIT_S)) if v})
        try:
            status, body = request("GET", f"/api/events/pull?{query}", timeout=PULL_WAIT_S + 15)
        except urllib.error.URLError:  # no connection was made (refused): an HTTP status returns from request()
            if not reached:
                return None
            time.sleep(RETRY_S)
            continue
        except (OSError, http.client.HTTPException):  # a server took the poll and the connection dropped
            reached = True
            time.sleep(RETRY_S)
            continue
        reached = True
        if status == 200 and body.get("text"):
            return str(body.get("id") or ""), str(body["text"]), session
        if status in STOP:
            if follow and process_session(pid) not in (None, session):
                continue  # main followed /clear while this poll for the session it left waited: poll for the new one
            return None
        if status != 204:
            time.sleep(RETRY_S)
    return None


def ack(cwd: str, session: str, event_id: str, terminal: bool = False) -> None:
    try:
        request("POST", "/api/events/ack", {"cwd": cwd, "session": session, "id": event_id, "terminal": terminal})
    except (OSError, http.client.HTTPException):
        pass


def watch(inp: dict, held=None) -> int:
    """The asyncRewake hook (module note); `held`, the session's lock, which the waker on local transport took before a
    press turned its session's transport to the server (watch_files)."""
    session = str(inp.get("session_id") or "")
    if inp.get("agent_id") or not session:
        return 0
    held = held or lock(session)
    if held is None:
        return 0
    cwd = folder(inp)
    pid = claude_pid()
    got = pull(cwd, session, time.monotonic() + LIFETIME_S, pid)
    if got is None:
        return 0
    if process_session(pid) not in (None, session):
        return 0  # /clear while the event came: neither written nor acknowledged, so the new session gets it
    sys.stderr.write(got[1] + "\n")
    sys.stderr.flush()
    ack(cwd, session, got[0], terminal=True)
    return WAKE


def permission(inp: dict, local) -> int:
    """The PermissionRequest hook (module note): after a press, the server hears that a prompt waits in the terminal;
    on local transport (`local`, the workspace folder) no one does. It prints nothing and decides nothing, so Claude
    Code asks in its own dialog."""
    if local is not None or server() is None:
        return 0
    body = {"cwd": folder(inp), "session": str(inp.get("session_id") or "") or None,
            "tool_name": str(inp.get("tool_name") or ""), "tool_input": inp.get("tool_input"),
            "agent_id": inp.get("agent_id") or None}
    try:
        request("POST", "/api/events/permission", body, timeout=PERMISSION_WAIT_S)
    except (OSError, http.client.HTTPException):
        pass
    return 0


def held(inp: dict) -> int:
    """The held hook (module note)."""
    if inp.get("agent_id"):
        return 0
    body = {"cwd": folder(inp), "session": str(inp.get("session_id") or "") or None}
    try:
        status, answer = request("POST", "/api/events/held", body, timeout=HELD_WAIT_S)
    except (OSError, http.client.HTTPException):
        return 0
    text, said = (str(answer.get("text") or ""), str(answer.get("terminal") or "")) if status == 200 else ("", "")
    out: dict = {"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": "UserPromptSubmit", "additionalContext": text}} if text else {}
    if said:
        out["systemMessage"] = said
    if out:
        print(json.dumps(out))
    return 0


def mode(inp: dict) -> int:
    """The mode hook (module note)."""
    ws = local_ws(inp)
    if ws is not None:
        return mode_files(inp, ws)
    if server() is None or inp.get("agent_id"):
        return 0
    said = [link_lines(str(inp.get("session_id") or ""))] if inp.get("hook_event_name") == "Stop" else []
    if inp.get("permission_mode"):
        body = {"cwd": folder(inp), "session": str(inp.get("session_id") or "") or None,
                "permission_mode": str(inp["permission_mode"])}
        try:
            status, answer = request("POST", "/api/events/mode", body, timeout=AGENTS_WAIT_S)
        except (OSError, http.client.HTTPException):
            status, answer = 0, {}
        if status == 200:
            said.append(str(answer.get("terminal") or ""))
    show(said)
    return 0


def show(lines: list) -> None:
    """`lines`, those not empty, printed as the hook's systemMessage, one per line."""
    text = "\n".join(x for x in lines if x)
    if text:
        print(json.dumps({"systemMessage": text}))


def ws_name(url: str) -> str:
    """The workspace a dashboard link names (`?ws=`), '' for the start page."""
    return (urllib.parse.parse_qs(urllib.parse.urlsplit(url).query).get("ws") or [""])[0]


def link_lines(session: str) -> str:
    """The link /thimble left for `session`, with a sign-in code the server makes now (POST /api/ui/pair), and the lines
    left after it, which the file then no longer holds (module note). The file's first line is the link, and empty when
    the server left only notes (app/session.py tell_terminal). Without a code, the line that says how to sign a browser
    in comes first in the notes. '' when nothing was left."""
    name = "".join(ch for ch in session if ch.isalnum() or ch in "-_")
    if not name:
        return ""
    path = home() / "links" / name
    try:
        text = path.read_text("utf-8")
        path.unlink()
    except OSError:
        return ""
    first, _, rest = text.partition("\n")
    url = first.strip()
    notes = [x for x in rest.splitlines() if x.strip()]
    if url:
        ws = ws_name(url)
        try:
            status, answer = request("POST", "/api/ui/pair", {"ws": ws}, timeout=PAIR_WAIT_S)
        except (OSError, http.client.HTTPException):
            status, answer = 0, {}
        code = answer.get("code") if status == 200 else None
        if isinstance(code, str) and code:
            url += "#p=" + code
        else:
            notes.insert(0, NO_CODE_LINE)
    return "\n".join(([f"thimble: {url}"] if url else []) + notes)


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- local transport


FILE_TICK_S = 0.5  # how often the waker looks at the event queue on local transport
MAIN_WAIT_S = 3.0  # how long the waker of a new session waits for --rekey to record that it is main's


def events():
    """app/event_files.py from the tree this plugin copy belongs to."""
    files()
    from app import event_files  # noqa: PLC0415 — standard library only

    return event_files


FILE_LOOK_TICKS = 4  # the waker takes again at least every this many ticks, the queue file changed or not


def watch_files(inp: dict, ws: Path) -> int:
    """The waker on local transport (module note): the oldest event for this session that no watcher has taken, from the
    queue, written to stderr with exit 2; 0 in a subagent, for a session with no marker (thimble is not on in it),
    when another waker holds the session's lock, and when the `claude` process has moved to another session or exited.
    Once a press turned this session's transport to the server, it pulls from the server with the lock it holds (watch):
    another hook's waker exits on that lock, and while main is idle no other hook runs. A new session's waker first
    waits up to MAIN_WAIT_S for --rekey to record a /clear's move to it, since main's events name no session."""
    session = str(inp.get("session_id") or "")
    if not session or inp.get("agent_id") or not (home() / "up" / f"{_safe(session)}.active").exists():
        return 0  # a subagent's hook, or a session thimble is not on in
    sf = files()
    if session not in sf.peers(ws):
        is_main(ws, session, MAIN_WAIT_S)
    held_lock = lock(session)
    if held_lock is None:
        return 0
    ef = events()
    pid = claude_pid()
    path = ef.queue_path(ws)
    seen = None
    ticks = 0
    until = time.monotonic() + LIFETIME_S
    while time.monotonic() < until:
        if pid and not alive(pid):
            return 0
        now = process_session(pid)
        if now and now != session:
            return 0
        try:
            st = path.stat()
            stamp = (st.st_mtime_ns, st.st_size)
        except OSError:
            stamp = None
        ticks += 1
        if stamp != seen or ticks % FILE_LOOK_TICKS == 0:  # with no queue file too: a press writes none
            seen = stamp
            if sf.transport(ws, session) != sf.LOCAL:
                return watch(inp, held_lock)
            got = ef.take(ws, session)
            if got is not None:
                sys.stderr.write(str(got.get("text") or "") + "\n")
                sys.stderr.flush()
                return WAKE
        time.sleep(FILE_TICK_S)
    return 0


def stream_files(args: list[str], ws: Path) -> int:
    """The Monitor route on local transport: every event of main's session from the queue, one block of lines each,
    until main's `claude` process exits, the session is no longer main's, or a press turned its transport to the
    server."""
    def arg(name: str) -> str:
        return args[args.index(name) + 1] if name in args and args.index(name) + 1 < len(args) else ""

    session = arg("--session")
    ef, sf = events(), files()
    pid = claude_pid()
    while True:
        if pid and not alive(pid):
            return 0
        session = process_session(pid) or session
        if not session or sf.main_session(ws) != session or sf.transport(ws, session) != sf.LOCAL:
            return 0
        got = ef.take(ws, session)
        if got is None:
            time.sleep(FILE_TICK_S)
            continue
        sys.stdout.write(fit(str(got.get("id") or ""), str(got.get("text") or "")) + "\n")
        sys.stdout.flush()


def held_files(inp: dict, ws: Path) -> int:
    """The held hook on local transport: the session's held events as the prompt's added context, and as its
    systemMessage the lines of the events the waker wrote out, the held events' and those that send main no event,
    less those the terminal's own rows already say (app/event_files.py TOLD_IN_CHAT). Main's held events name no
    session; a peer's name it."""
    session = str(inp.get("session_id") or "")
    if inp.get("agent_id") or not session:
        return 0
    ef = events()
    riders = ef.pop_held(ws, None if is_main(ws, session) else session)
    text = ef.meanwhile(riders)
    lines = [*ef.unshown(ws, session), ef.said(riders)]
    said = "\n".join(dict.fromkeys(x for x in lines if x))
    out: dict = {"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": "UserPromptSubmit", "additionalContext": text}} if text else {}
    if said:
        out["systemMessage"] = said
    if out:
        print(json.dumps(out))
    return 0


def mode_files(inp: dict, ws: Path) -> int:
    """The mode hook on local transport: main's permission mode recorded in subagents.json (app/subagent_files.py
    record_mode); when it turns into or out of Manual mode (MANUAL_MODES), the backend's `mode-notice` call, which shows
    or clears the `manual-mode` notice in thimble-term's band (app/local_hooks.py); and on main's Stop the backend's
    `main-stop` call. It prints nothing, and records nothing for a peer."""
    session = str(inp.get("session_id") or "")
    if inp.get("agent_id") or not session or not is_main(ws, session):
        return 0
    sf = files()
    mode = str(inp.get("permission_mode") or "")
    if mode:
        with sf.update(ws) as state:
            before = str((state.get("main") or {}).get("permission_mode") or "")
            changed = sf.record_mode(state, session, mode)
        if changed and (mode in sf.MANUAL_MODES) != (before in sf.MANUAL_MODES):
            spawn_local("mode-notice", inp)
    if inp.get("hook_event_name") == "Stop":
        spawn_local("main-stop", inp)
    return 0


# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- the hooks of thimble's agents


def files():
    """app/subagent_files.py from the tree this plugin copy belongs to (module note)."""
    tree = os.environ.get("THIMBLE_APP_DIR") or str(Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2])
    backend = str(Path(tree) / "backend")
    if backend not in sys.path:
        sys.path.insert(0, backend)
    from app import subagent_files  # noqa: PLC0415

    return subagent_files


def workspace(inp: dict):
    """(app/subagent_files.py, the workspace folder of the session's folder), or (the module, None) for a folder of no
    workspace."""
    sf = files()
    return sf, sf.workspace_folder(folder(inp))


# app/local_hooks.py from the tree bin/thimble-python runs (it exports THIMBLE_APP_DIR), whichever copy of the plugin
# this is
LOCAL_HOOKS = ("import os, sys; sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.environ['THIMBLE_APP_DIR'], 'backend')); "
               "from app.local_hooks import main; sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))")


def local_ws(inp: dict):
    """The workspace folder of the session's folder when the hook's session runs on local transport (module note:
    app/subagent_files.py transport, read from launch.json); None after a press, and for a folder of no workspace."""
    sf, ws = workspace(inp)
    if ws is None:
        return None
    return ws if sf.transport(ws, str(inp.get("session_id") or "") or None) == sf.LOCAL else None


def on_local(sf, ws: Path, inp: dict) -> bool:
    """Whether the hook's session runs on local transport in the workspace folder `ws` (local_ws)."""
    return sf.transport(ws, str(inp.get("session_id") or "") or None) == sf.LOCAL


def spawn_local(kind: str, inp: dict) -> None:
    """The backend's call for a hook's record on local transport (module note): `thimble-python -m app.local_hooks <kind>`
    with the hook's input on its stdin, in the session's folder, detached, and not waited for."""
    import subprocess  # noqa: PLC0415 — only the hooks on local transport start a process

    here = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
    try:
        proc = subprocess.Popen([str(here / "thimble-python"), "-c", LOCAL_HOOKS, kind], stdin=subprocess.PIPE,
                                stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, cwd=folder(inp) or None,
                                start_new_session=True, close_fds=True)
    except OSError:
        return
    try:
        proc.stdin.write(json.dumps(inp).encode("utf-8"))
        proc.stdin.close()
    except OSError:
        pass


def is_main(ws: Path, session: str, wait_s: float = 0.0) -> bool:
    """Whether `session` is main's (app/subagent_files.py main_session), waiting up to `wait_s` for the
    --rekey hook of a /clear to record a move to it."""
    sf = files()
    end = time.monotonic() + wait_s
    while True:
        if session and sf.main_session(ws) == session:
            return True
        if time.monotonic() >= end:
            return False
        time.sleep(0.1)


def post(path: str, body: dict, timeout: float = AGENTS_WAIT_S) -> dict:
    """The server's JSON answer to `body` posted to `path`, {} when no server runs or it does not answer."""
    if server() is None:
        return {}
    try:
        status, answer = request("POST", path, body, timeout=timeout)
    except (OSError, http.client.HTTPException):
        return {}
    return answer if status == 200 else {}


def deny(reason: str) -> None:
    print(json.dumps({"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": "PreToolUse", "permissionDecision": "deny",
                                             "permissionDecisionReason": reason}}))


# the types of thimble's seven roles (app/subagent_files.py ROLES, which a test holds this to): a start of one is denied
# when the check itself fails, since a hook that fails lets the call run, and no such start may run unasked
ROLE_TYPES = tuple(f"thimble:{r}" for r in ("orientation", "critic", "writer", "view-builder", "view-reviewer", "check",
                                            "dev-ticket"))
CHECK_FAILED = "thimble could not check this start against the analyst's requests, so it does not run"
PLUGIN_CALL = "toolu_plugin_"  # app/subagent_files.py PLUGIN_CALL: a call thimble's module made, a click's


def agent_check(inp: dict) -> int:
    """The agent-check hook (module note)."""
    tool_input = inp.get("tool_input") if isinstance(inp.get("tool_input"), dict) else {}
    if not tool_input:
        return 0
    term = False
    try:
        sf, ws = workspace(inp)
        if ws is None:
            return 0
        term = on_local(sf, ws, inp)
        with sf.update(ws) as state:
            reason = sf.check_call(state, inp)
            if reason is None and term and not inp.get("agent_id") and str(inp.get("tool_name") or "") in sf.AGENT_TOOLS:
                # a second fork of a thread (the server's fork_check); a call let through is kept by its tool_use id
                reason = sf.fork_check(state, tool_input, ws, inp.get("tool_use_id"))
        if reason is not None:
            reason = reason or sf.hint("agent-check-exact") or "thimble did not ask for this call"
    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 — fail closed for a start of one of thimble's roles, open for anything else
        if str(inp.get("tool_name") or "") not in ("Agent", "Task") or \
                str(tool_input.get("subagent_type") or "") not in ROLE_TYPES:
            return 0
        reason = CHECK_FAILED
    if not inp.get("agent_id") and str(inp.get("tool_use_id") or "").startswith(PLUGIN_CALL):
        # a click's call through the module carries main's permission mode as it runs, which thimble otherwise hears
        # only at main's turns: a shift+tab while main is idle shows in the browser from here (live check L21)
        mode(inp)
    if reason is not None:
        deny(reason)
        return 0
    if term or inp.get("agent_id") or str(inp.get("tool_name") or "") not in sf.AGENT_TOOLS:
        return 0
    answer = post("/api/bg/agent-check", {"cwd": folder(inp), "agent_id": None, "tool_use_id": inp.get("tool_use_id"),
                                          "tool_input": tool_input})
    if answer.get("deny"):
        deny(str(answer.get("reason") or ""))
    return 0


SCRATCH_PREFIX = "tmp_"  # app/work_files.py: the scratch folders a run's end deletes


def subagent_start(inp: dict) -> int:
    """The SubagentStart hook (module note): the agent registered, then the scratch line for a descendant of one of
    thimble's agents, a folder of its own in its ancestor's work folder (## session-scratch). An agent of one of
    thimble's roles whose own start is not known yet (main started two or more of its type in one turn) waits for the
    sign that names its call (app/subagent_files.py settle); on local transport the backend's call still runs, so that
    its pass reads main's transcript, where the call's result names the agent. An agent that took its start can leave
    an unsettled agent one start, which it takes too (`settled`): the backend's call runs for it as well."""
    sf, ws = workspace(inp)
    if ws is None:
        return 0
    settled: list = []
    with sf.update(ws) as state:
        entry = sf.register(state, inp, settled)
        unsettled = sf.unsettled(state, str(inp.get("agent_id") or "")) is not None
    if entry is None and not unsettled:
        return 0
    if on_local(sf, ws, inp):
        spawn_local("started", inp)
    elif entry is not None:
        post("/api/subagents/started", {"cwd": folder(inp), "hook": inp})
    tell_started(sf, ws, inp, settled)
    if entry is None:
        return 0
    work = entry.get("work") if entry.get("descendant") else None
    agent = "".join(ch for ch in str(inp.get("agent_id") or "") if ch.isalnum() or ch in "-_")[:64]
    if work and agent:
        scratch = Path(str(work)) / f"{SCRATCH_PREFIX}{agent}"
        try:
            scratch.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        except OSError:
            return 0
        text = sf.hint("session-scratch", folder=str(scratch))
        if text:
            print(json.dumps({"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": "SubagentStart", "additionalContext": text}}))
    return 0


def tell_started(sf, ws: Path, inp: dict, agents: list) -> None:
    """The backend's call for each agent in `agents` that took up its start after its own SubagentStart hook ran (app/
    subagent_files.py settle): its chat and its role's start handler, as the server's started route, or on local
    transport the local hooks' `started`, gives them."""
    for agent in agents:
        hook = {"hook_event_name": "SubagentStart", "session_id": inp.get("session_id"), "cwd": inp.get("cwd"),
                "agent_id": agent}
        if on_local(sf, ws, inp):
            spawn_local("started", hook)
        else:
            post("/api/subagents/started", {"cwd": folder(inp), "hook": hook})


def settle_launch(inp: dict) -> None:
    """The PostToolUse hook of an Agent call, main's or a subagent's, that launched one of thimble's agents: Claude
    Code's answer names the agent (app/subagent_files.py launched_agent), which takes up the start the call claimed, or
    takes it up at its SubagentStart when that hook has not run yet (settle)."""
    sf = files()
    agent = sf.launched_agent(inp)
    if not agent:
        return
    _, ws = workspace(inp)
    if ws is None:
        return
    with sf.update(ws) as state:
        settled = sf.settle(state, agent, str(inp.get("tool_use_id") or ""))
    tell_started(sf, ws, inp, settled)


def subagent_stop(inp: dict) -> int:
    """The SubagentStop hook (module note): a registered agent's turn ended; or the turn of another subagent (a
    thread's fork) ended, and the typed starts its start tool calls asked for that its Agent call never made are
    refused (subagent_files.refuse_unclaimed)."""
    if inp.get("stop_hook_active") or not str(inp.get("agent_type") or ""):
        return 0
    sf, ws = workspace(inp)
    if ws is None:
        return 0
    with sf.update(ws) as state:
        entry = sf.record_stop(state, inp)
        refused = sf.refuse_unclaimed(state, inp) if entry is None else []
    if on_local(sf, ws, inp):  # every subagent's turn end: the mirror reads a thread's fork too
        spawn_local("stopped", {**inp, "refused": refused})
    elif entry is not None or refused:
        post("/api/subagents/stopped", {"cwd": folder(inp), "hook": {**inp, "refused": refused}})
    return 0


def caller(inp: dict) -> int:
    """The caller hook (module note): the line of callers.jsonl that names the agent making a thimble call, or no agent
    for main's own call, and the parent of a descendant whose nested start was ambiguous, from its meta.json."""
    agent = str(inp.get("agent_id") or "")
    sf, ws = workspace(inp)
    if ws is None:
        return 0
    sf.add_caller(ws, str(inp.get("tool_use_id") or ""), agent, str(inp.get("agent_type") or ""))
    if not agent:
        return 0
    entry = sf.registry(sf.read(ws)).get(agent)
    if isinstance(entry, dict) and entry.get("candidates") and not entry.get("parent"):
        parent = parent_of(inp, agent)
        if parent:
            with sf.update(ws) as state:
                sf.resolve_parent(state, agent, parent)
    return 0


def parent_of(inp: dict, agent: str) -> str:
    """`parentAgentId` in the agent's meta.json, beside its transcript under main's session folder."""
    main = str(inp.get("transcript_path") or "")
    sid = str(inp.get("session_id") or "")
    if not main or not sid:
        return ""
    meta = Path(main).parent / sid / "subagents" / f"agent-{agent}.meta.json"
    try:
        data = json.loads(meta.read_text("utf-8"))
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return ""
    return str(data.get("parentAgentId") or "") if isinstance(data, dict) else ""


def denied(inp: dict) -> int:
    """The PermissionDenied hook (module note): R1."""
    sf, ws = workspace(inp)
    if ws is None:
        return 0
    with sf.update(ws) as state:
        hit = sf.record_denied(state, inp)
    if hit is not None and on_local(sf, ws, inp):
        spawn_local("denied", {**inp, "request": hit[0]})
    elif hit is not None:
        post("/api/subagents/denied", {"cwd": folder(inp), "hook": {**inp, "request": hit[0]}})
    return 0


END_POST_S = 1.0  # the SessionEnd hook's post is sent and not waited for longer than this


def end(inp: dict) -> int:
    """The SessionEnd hook (module note): main's end recorded, with its `claude` process (the --rekey that follows a
    /clear finds it by it); on clear and resume only that, since the new session waits for this hook."""
    if inp.get("agent_id"):
        return 0
    sf, ws = workspace(inp)
    if ws is None:
        return 0
    with sf.update(ws) as state:
        sf.record_end(state, {**inp, "pid": claude_pid()})
    if str(inp.get("reason") or "") in ("clear", "resume"):
        return 0
    if on_local(sf, ws, inp):
        spawn_local("end", inp)
    else:
        post("/api/subagents/end", {"cwd": folder(inp), "hook": inp}, timeout=END_POST_S)
    return 0


def rekey(inp: dict) -> int:
    """The SessionStart hook for clear and resume (module note): the session that ended in this `claude` process (its
    SessionEnd record) moves to the new session: its marker and session files (rekey_marker), and the agents it left
    running; main stays main through the move, and a peer stays a peer."""
    source = str(inp.get("source") or "")
    if inp.get("agent_id") or source not in ("clear", "resume"):
        return 0
    sf, ws = workspace(inp)
    if ws is None:
        return 0
    new = str(inp.get("session_id") or "")
    pid = claude_pid()
    with sf.update(ws) as state:
        last = state.get("main_end") if isinstance(state.get("main_end"), dict) else {}
        old = str(last.get("session") or "") if not pid or not last.get("pid") or last.get("pid") == pid else ""
        was_main = bool(old) and sf.main_session(ws, state) == old
        moved = sf.rekey(state, old, new, main=was_main) if old else []
    if old:
        try:
            rekey_marker(old, new, source, ws)
        except OSError:
            pass
    if old and on_local(sf, ws, {"session_id": new}):
        spawn_local("rekey", {**inp, "old": old, "moved": moved})
    elif old:
        post("/api/subagents/rekey", {"cwd": folder(inp), "hook": {**inp, "old": old, "moved": moved}})
    return 0


def _safe(sid: str) -> str:
    return "".join(ch for ch in sid if ch.isalnum() or ch in "-_")


def _write_private(path: Path, data: bytes) -> None:
    tmp = path.with_name(f".{path.name}.{os.getpid()}.tmp")
    fd = os.open(tmp, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_TRUNC, 0o600)
    try:
        os.write(fd, data)
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def rekey_marker(old: str, new: str, source: str, ws: Path) -> bool:
    """The session marker of `old` and its folder of session files (<home>/up/<old>.active, <home>/up/<old>/) copied to
    `new` (module note), under the new session's lock (<home>/up/<new>.lock, activation's): for /resume every file as it
    was, and the session's coverage facts (<ws>/coverage/<old>.jsonl); for /clear the guidance's record emptied
    (guide.json) and a new guide marker (guide-marker), so the guidance is owed again, and no coverage facts. The marker
    keeps `mod`. Nothing when `new` has a marker already (the terminal UI's activation ran first) or `old` has none.
    True when it copied."""
    o, n = _safe(old), _safe(new)
    up = home() / "up"
    if not o or not n or o == n or not (up / f"{o}.active").is_file():
        return False
    up.mkdir(mode=0o700, parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    with open(up / f"{n}.lock", "a") as held:
        fcntl.flock(held, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        if (up / f"{n}.active").exists():
            return False
        src, dst = up / o, up / n
        if src.is_dir():
            dst.mkdir(mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
            for f in src.iterdir():
                if not f.is_file() or f.is_symlink():
                    continue
                if source == "clear" and f.name == "guide.json":
                    data = b"{}"
                elif source == "clear" and f.name == "guide-marker":
                    data = secrets.token_hex(4).encode()
                else:
                    data = f.read_bytes()
                _write_private(dst / f.name, data)
        if source == "clear" and not (dst / "guide-marker").exists():
            dst.mkdir(mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)
            _write_private(dst / "guide-marker", secrets.token_hex(4).encode())
        if source == "resume":
            facts = Path(ws) / "coverage" / f"{o}.jsonl"
            if facts.is_file():
                (Path(ws) / "coverage" / f"{n}.jsonl").write_bytes(facts.read_bytes())
        _write_private(up / f"{n}.active", (up / f"{o}.active").read_bytes())
    return True


WORK_BUDGET = 2 * 1000 ** 3  # bytes: app/agent_session.py WORK_BUDGET
CHECK_S = 30.0  # the work folder is measured at most this often
BUDGET_FILE = ".thimble-budget.json"  # in the work folder: when it was measured, and the last budget step warned of
WALK_MAX = 500_000  # the entries of the folder counted at most, so that a measure stays short


def size_of(work: Path) -> int:
    """The bytes of the files under `work`, links counted as links and never followed."""
    total = n = 0
    for root, dirs, names in os.walk(work):
        for name in names:
            try:
                total += os.lstat(os.path.join(root, name)).st_size
            except OSError:
                pass
        n += len(names) + len(dirs)
        if n > WALK_MAX:
            break
    return total


def _size(n: int) -> str:
    return f"{n / 1e9:.1f} GB" if n >= 1e9 else f"{n / 1e6:.0f} MB"


def budget_line(work: Path, budget: int, text: str) -> str:
    """The work-budget warning for `work` when it grew past another whole `budget` since the last one, at most every
    CHECK_S ('' otherwise); `{size}`, `{budget}` and `{folder}` in `text` filled."""
    if budget <= 0 or not work.is_dir() or not text:
        return ""
    state_file = work / BUDGET_FILE
    try:
        state = json.loads(state_file.read_text("utf-8"))
        checked, warned = float(state["checked"]), int(state["warned"])
    except (OSError, ValueError, TypeError, KeyError):
        checked, warned = 0.0, 0
    now = time.time()
    if now - checked < CHECK_S:
        return ""
    size = size_of(work)
    step = size // budget
    say = step > warned
    try:
        tmp = state_file.with_name(f"{BUDGET_FILE}.{os.getpid()}.tmp")
        tmp.write_text(json.dumps({"checked": now, "size": size, "warned": step if say else min(warned, step)}), "utf-8")
        os.replace(tmp, state_file)
    except OSError:
        return ""
    if not say:
        return ""
    return text.replace("{size}", _size(size)).replace("{budget}", _size(budget)).replace("{folder}", str(work))


THIMBLE_PREFIXES = ("mcp__plugin_thimble_thimble__", "mcp__thimble__", "mcp__thimble-")  # app/calls.py THIMBLE_PREFIXES
PLUMBING = ("ToolSearch",)  # app/session.py PLUMBING_TOOLS


def agents_hook(inp: dict) -> int:
    """The agents hook (module note)."""
    agent = str(inp.get("agent_id") or "")
    name = str(inp.get("tool_name") or "")
    if name in ("Agent", "Task"):
        try:
            settle_launch(inp)
        except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 — the agent's other signs settle it; main still gets the note below
            pass
    if not agent and name in ("Agent", "Task"):
        return launched_hook(inp)
    if not agent or not name:
        return 0
    sf, ws = workspace(inp)
    if ws is None:
        return 0
    reg = sf.registry(sf.read(ws))
    entry = reg.get(agent)
    if not isinstance(entry, dict):
        return 0
    root_id = agent if entry.get("role") in sf.ROLES else str(entry.get("root") or "")
    root = reg.get(root_id) if root_id else None
    if not isinstance(root, dict):
        return 0
    if root.get("role") == "critic" and isinstance(reg.get(str(root.get("parent") or "")), dict):
        root_id = str(root["parent"])  # the critic's calls are numbered in its orientation's sequence
        root = reg[root_id]
    lines = []
    term = on_local(sf, ws, inp)
    if root.get("role") == "orientation" and inp.get("tool_use_id") and not name.startswith(THIMBLE_PREFIXES) \
            and name not in PLUMBING:
        if term:
            ref = call_ref(ws, str(root.get("chat") or ""), inp, None if agent == root_id else agent)
            if ref:
                lines.append(sf.hint("call-ref", ref=ref))
        else:
            body = {"session": str(root.get("key") or ""), "tool_use_id": inp.get("tool_use_id"), "tool_name": name,
                    "tool_input": inp.get("tool_input"), "agent_id": None if agent == root_id else agent}
            answer = post(f"/api/ws/{urllib.parse.quote(ws.name, safe='')}/calls/ref", body)
            if answer.get("context"):
                lines.append(str(answer["context"]))
    work = entry.get("work") or root.get("work")
    if name == "Bash" and work:
        warn = budget_line(Path(str(work)), WORK_BUDGET, sf.hint("work-budget", folder="{folder}", size="{size}",
                                                                  budget="{budget}"))
        if warn:
            lines.append(warn)
    if lines:
        event = str(inp.get("hook_event_name") or "PostToolUse")
        print(json.dumps({"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": event, "additionalContext": "\n".join(lines)}}))
    return 0


def launched_hook(inp: dict) -> int:
    """Main's own Agent call launched a thread's fork or one of thimble's agents: the note that ends the turn on it
    (app/subagent_files.py launched_note), as added context alone, with no systemMessage, so the terminal draws no row."""
    sf, ws = workspace(inp)
    if ws is None:
        return 0
    text = sf.launched_note(inp)
    if text:
        print(json.dumps({"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": "PostToolUse", "additionalContext": text}}))
    return 0


def call_ref(ws: Path, chat: str, inp: dict, agent: str | None) -> str:
    """Local transport: the call numbered in the orientation's sequence (app/calls_file.py number, which the mirror's
    numbering shares) and its ref, `call:<chat>/<n>`, as the server's calls/ref route answers it; '' while the
    orientation has no chat yet."""
    if not chat:
        return ""
    files()
    try:
        from app import calls_file  # noqa: PLC0415 — standard library only
    except ImportError:
        return ""
    try:
        n = calls_file.number(ws, chat, str(inp.get("tool_use_id") or ""), str(inp.get("tool_name") or ""),
                              inp.get("tool_input"), agent)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return ""
    return f"call:{chat}/{n}"


def scratch(inp: dict, args: list[str]) -> int:
    """An extension's program session's SubagentStart hook: the subagent's own scratch folder in the session's work
    folder (--work), named in --text's `{folder}`."""
    def arg(name: str) -> str:
        return args[args.index(name) + 1] if name in args and args.index(name) + 1 < len(args) else ""

    work, text = arg("--work"), arg("--text")
    agent = "".join(ch for ch in str(inp.get("agent_id") or "") if ch.isalnum() or ch in "-_")[:64]
    if not work or not text or not agent:
        return 0
    folder_ = Path(work) / f"{SCRATCH_PREFIX}{agent}"
    try:
        folder_.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    except OSError:
        return 0
    print(json.dumps({"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": "SubagentStart",
                                             "additionalContext": text.replace("{folder}", str(folder_))}}))
    return 0


def budget(args: list[str]) -> int:
    """An extension's program session's PostToolUse hook of Bash: the work-budget warning for --work (budget_line)."""
    def arg(name: str) -> str:
        return args[args.index(name) + 1] if name in args and args.index(name) + 1 < len(args) else ""

    try:
        n = int(arg("--budget"))
    except ValueError:
        return 0
    line = budget_line(Path(arg("--work")), n, arg("--text")) if arg("--work") else ""
    if line:
        print(json.dumps({"hookSpecificOutput": {"hookEventName": "PostToolUse", "additionalContext": line}}))
    return 0


def printing(pid: int | None) -> bool:
    """Whether the `claude` process `pid` runs with -p or --print (module note, the waker)."""
    if not pid:
        return False
    try:
        argv = Path(f"/proc/{pid}/cmdline").read_bytes().split(b"\0")
        args = [a.decode("utf-8", "replace") for a in argv if a]
    except OSError:
        import subprocess  # noqa: PLC0415 — macOS: no /proc
        try:
            out = subprocess.run(["ps", "-o", "args=", "-p", str(pid)], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=2).stdout
        except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
            return False
        args = out.split()
    return any(a in ("-p", "--print") or a.startswith("--print=") for a in args[1:])


def units(s: str) -> int:
    """The length of `s` as Claude Code counts it (JavaScript): UTF-16 code units, two for a character beyond U+FFFF."""
    return len(s.encode("utf-16-le")) // 2


def wrap(line: str, at: re.Pattern = SPACE) -> list[str]:
    """`line` as lines of at most LINE_CHARS units (module note), each broken at the last match of `at` that fits, else
    inside a word."""
    out: list[str] = []
    while units(line) > LINE_CHARS:
        n = LINE_CHARS
        while units(line[:n]) > LINE_CHARS:
            n -= 1
        cuts = [m for m in at.finditer(line) if 0 < m.start() <= n]
        if cuts:
            out.append(line[: cuts[-1].start()])
            line = line[cuts[-1].end():]
        else:
            out.append(line[:n])
            line = line[n:]
    return [*out, line]


def fit(event_id: str, text: str) -> str:
    """The event as one Monitor event (module note): every line wrapped under LINE_CHARS, and an event longer than
    STREAM_CHARS cut inside its body with the whole saved."""
    if len(text) > STREAM_CHARS:
        text = cut(event_id, text)
    head, _, rest = text.partition("\n")
    return "\n".join([*wrap(head, ATTR_BREAK), *(part for line in rest.split("\n") for part in wrap(line))])


def cut(event_id: str, text: str) -> str:
    """The event cut inside its body before STREAM_CHARS, with a line saying where the whole of it is saved."""
    head, _, rest = text.partition("\n")
    body = rest[: -len(END_TAG)].rstrip("\n") if rest.endswith(END_TAG) else rest
    path = home() / "events" / f"{''.join(ch for ch in event_id if ch.isalnum()) or int(time.time())}.txt"
    try:
        path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        path.write_text(text, "utf-8")
    except OSError:
        pass
    note = CUT_NOTE.format(path=path)
    keep = max(0, STREAM_CHARS - len(head) - len(note) - len(END_TAG) - 8)
    return f"{head}\n{body[:keep].rstrip()}\n…\n{note}\n{END_TAG}"


def stream(args: list[str]) -> int:
    """The Monitor route (module note): every event of the session, one block of lines each, until the server says to
    stop."""
    def arg(name: str) -> str:
        return args[args.index(name) + 1] if name in args and args.index(name) + 1 < len(args) else ""

    cwd, session = arg("--cwd") or os.getcwd(), arg("--session")
    pid = claude_pid()
    while True:
        got = pull(cwd, session, time.monotonic() + LIFETIME_S, pid, follow=True)
        if got is None:
            try:
                request("GET", "/api/health", timeout=3.0, proven=False)
            except (OSError, http.client.HTTPException):
                time.sleep(RETRY_S)  # the server is down: the Monitor waits for it rather than ending
                continue
            return 0
        sys.stdout.write(fit(got[0], got[1]) + "\n")
        sys.stdout.flush()
        ack(cwd, got[2], got[0])


FILE_FIRST = {"--agent-check": agent_check, "--subagent-start": subagent_start, "--subagent-stop": subagent_stop,
              "--caller": caller, "--denied": denied, "--end": end, "--rekey": rekey, "--agents": agents_hook}


def main() -> int:
    args = sys.argv[1:]
    try:
        if "--stream" in args:
            def arg(name: str) -> str:
                return args[args.index(name) + 1] if name in args and args.index(name) + 1 < len(args) else ""

            ws = local_ws({"cwd": arg("--cwd"), "session_id": arg("--session")})
            return stream(args) if ws is None else stream_files(args, ws)
        if "--scratch" in args:
            return scratch(hook_input(), args)
        if "--work-budget" in args:
            return budget(args)
        for flag, fn in FILE_FIRST.items():  # these write the workspace's files first, whatever the transport
            if flag in args:
                return fn(hook_input())
        inp = hook_input()
        ws = local_ws(inp)
        if "--permission" in args:
            return permission(inp, ws)  # decides nothing, on either transport (module note)
        if ws is not None:  # local transport: files only, no server (module note)
            if "--held" in args:
                return held_files(inp, ws)
            if "--mode" in args:
                return mode_files(inp, ws)
            if printing(claude_pid()):
                return 0
            return watch_files(inp, ws)
        if server() is None:  # no thimble server recorded: every other hook does nothing (module note)
            return 0
        if "--held" in args:
            return held(inp)
        if "--mode" in args:
            return mode(inp)
        if printing(claude_pid()):
            return 0  # the waker in `claude -p` (module note)
        return watch(inp)
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        return 0
    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001 — a failure wakes nothing: an exit 2 would show its traceback to the model
        return 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
